frontend: render-pass memory barriers in panel-sized surface passes, a switch and a console line (piano-metal-barriers)

The VM's frontend leaves out every render-pass memory barrier (RenderBox's in-encoder coverage read-backs, which the bridge implements
by splitting the pass) in a pass whose colour target is an IOSurface of more than 4 Mpx: there a barrier locked the Adreno up at
every 3200x2136 login in the VM (msm hangcheck; the bridge's split pass loads and stores the whole surface in GMEM). Natively the
panel is 3200x2136 and every full-screen window's surface is past that limit (SecurityAgent's login UI included), while every pass
renders in sysmem (the bridge's pipelines carry the colour-attachment feedback-loop flag, which disables GMEM in Turnip), where a
split costs no GMEM load or store. Now:
- piano-metal-barriers=all|small|none on the boot line (kern.bootargs), else the first word of /private/var/ngpu/debug/render-barriers
  (readable where the boot line is not, as Turnip's tu-debug), else none with com.droidvm.nmb-no-render-barrier as before, else small
  (the VM's rule, unchanged by default). A process whose policy is not small says so once on stderr.
- Each barrier left out in a panel-sized pass is an NBLOG line ("native-metal: render memory barrier left out in a N-pixel surface
  pass (M so far; piano-metal-barriers=all keeps them)"), rate-limited as every NBLOG on stderr: whether a client asks for them
  at the login window and on the desktop was never measured.
Applied by tooling/metal/build-turnip-a830.sh after 0001. MIT, as the file.

--- a/frontend.mm
+++ b/frontend.mm
@@ -2771,14 +2771,53 @@
 // read-backs are in offscreen targets (icons, glyphs, their atlases -- some larger than 4 Mpx: all blank when every big pass
 // lost its barriers), which keep them.
 static constexpr uint64_t kBarrierMaxPassPixels = 4000000;
-static bool nbRenderBarriers() {
- static int on = -1;
- if (on < 0) on = access("/Library/Preferences/com.droidvm.nmb-no-render-barrier", F_OK) != 0;
- return on;
+// UniXNU-piano (tooling/metal/turnip-a830/frontend 0002): which render-pass barriers are kept, read once per process.
+//   all   every one, panel-sized surface passes included (natively every pass renders in sysmem, so the split costs no GMEM
+//         load and store of the whole surface: what the VM's hang was suspected of);
+//   small all but those in a panel-sized pass into an IOSurface (the VM's rule above; the default);
+//   none  no barrier at all (as com.droidvm.nmb-no-render-barrier).
+// From the boot argument piano-metal-barriers=all|small|none (kern.bootargs), else the first word of
+// /private/var/ngpu/debug/render-barriers (a sandboxed process that cannot read the boot line still reads that file, as Turnip's
+// tu-debug), else none while /Library/Preferences/com.droidvm.nmb-no-render-barrier exists, else small. A barrier left out in a
+// panel-sized pass is on stderr (NBLOG's rate limit: the first 8, then the 16th, 32nd, ... with the count).
+enum NBBarrierPolicy {NBBarriersNone,NBBarriersSmall,NBBarriersAll};
+static NBBarrierPolicy nbBarrierWord(const char *w,NBBarrierPolicy fallback) {
+ if(!strncmp(w,"all",3))return NBBarriersAll;
+ if(!strncmp(w,"small",5))return NBBarriersSmall;
+ if(!strncmp(w,"none",4))return NBBarriersNone;
+ return fallback;
 }
+static NBBarrierPolicy nbBarrierPolicy() {
+ static const NBBarrierPolicy policy=[]{
+  const char *from="the default";
+  NBBarrierPolicy p=NBBarriersSmall;
+  char args[1024]={};size_t size=sizeof args-1;
+  const char *at=nullptr;
+  if(!sysctlbyname("kern.bootargs",args,&size,NULL,0)) {
+   static const char key[]="piano-metal-barriers=";
+   for(const char *s=args;(s=strstr(s,key));s+=sizeof key-1)if(s==args || s[-1]==' '){at=s+sizeof key-1;break;}
+  }
+  if(at){p=nbBarrierWord(at,p);from="boot argument piano-metal-barriers";}
+  else if(FILE *f=fopen("/private/var/ngpu/debug/render-barriers","r")) {
+   char w[32]={};if(fscanf(f,"%31s",w)==1){p=nbBarrierWord(w,p);from="/private/var/ngpu/debug/render-barriers";}
+   fclose(f);
+  } else if(access("/Library/Preferences/com.droidvm.nmb-no-render-barrier",F_OK)==0){p=NBBarriersNone;from="com.droidvm.nmb-no-render-barrier";}
+  if(p!=NBBarriersSmall)NBLOG(@"native-metal: render-pass memory barriers: %s (from %s)",p==NBBarriersAll?"all":"none",from);
+  return p;
+ }();
+ return policy;
+}
+static bool nbRenderBarriers() {return nbBarrierPolicy()!=NBBarriersNone;}
 @implementation NBRenderEncoder
-// A panel-sized pass into an IOSurface (WindowServer's and the windows' framebuffers): no barrier there (see kBarrierMaxPassPixels).
-- (BOOL)barrierUnsafePass {return self.passPixels > kBarrierMaxPassPixels && (self.passKey >> 18 & 1);}
+// A panel-sized pass into an IOSurface (WindowServer's and the windows' framebuffers): no barrier there (see kBarrierMaxPassPixels)
+// unless piano-metal-barriers=all. Each one left out is on stderr (rate-limited), so a run shows whether a client asked for them.
+- (BOOL)barrierUnsafePass {
+ if(nbBarrierPolicy()==NBBarriersAll || !(self.passPixels > kBarrierMaxPassPixels && (self.passKey >> 18 & 1)))return NO;
+ static std::atomic<uint64_t> leftOut{0};
+ NBLOG(@"native-metal: render memory barrier left out in a %llu-pixel surface pass (%llu so far; piano-metal-barriers=all keeps them)",
+       (unsigned long long)self.passPixels,(unsigned long long)++leftOut);
+ return YES;
+}
 // Render-pass memory barriers (the bridge splits the pass): RenderBox reads back, in the same encoder, the coverage an earlier draw
 // accumulated in a render target; dropped, SwiftUI glyphs and IconRendering icons drew as blocks or nothing (piano, 2026-11-10).
 - (void)memoryBarrierWithScope:(MTLBarrierScope)scope afterStages:(MTLRenderStages)after beforeStages:(MTLRenderStages)before {
